# The gortex release this fleet pins to. One bare semver, no `v` prefix.
#
# WHY IT LIVES HERE. This pin used to be `pkgs/gortex.nix`, and `tier_gortex` in
# provision/lib/tiers.sh grepped the `version = "…"` line out of it on every box.
# That made a Nix package definition a live input to POSIX provisioning, which
# was already odd and became untenable when the NixOS tree was deleted on
# 2026-08-01 (see docs/2026-08-01-nixos-harvest.md). It is data, so it is a data
# file, and it sits under provision/ because the provisioner is what reads it.
#
# Readers: tier_gortex (provision/lib/tiers.sh) installs this version into
# ~/.local/bin; _touches_driver (scripts/converge.sh) treats a change here as a
# reprovision trigger so a bump actually reaches every box. Writer:
# scripts/update-gortex.sh (`just update-gortex`).
#
# It is also written UNATTENDED, by exactly one box: provision/gortex-autoupdate.sh
# runs weekly on latitude (tier_gortex_autoupdate, `server` profile only) and
# commits a bump here when upstream has a newer release that is at least 48h old.
# So a commit touching only this file may not have a human behind it — and
# reverting that commit is the fleet-wide rollback, which is why the bump is a
# commit rather than a box mutation. Two writers would race on the push; if you
# ever want a different box to publish, MOVE the tier, never copy it.
#
# The reader takes the first bare semver on a non-comment line, so this header is
# safe. Do NOT add a `v`.
0.63.2
